          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#finite_distributions"} Finite distributions
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#pushforward"} Pushforward
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#monad_structure"} Monad structure
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#see_also"} See also
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The distribution monad is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+spaces"} convex spaces
          %p
            It can be thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+monad"} finitary
            prototype of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monad"} probability monad
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#finite_distributions Finite distributions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a set. Define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D X
            as the set whose elements are functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:X\to[0,1]
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(x)\ne 0
                for only finitely many
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{x\in X} p(x)=1
                \.
          %p Note that the sum above is finite if one excludes all the zero addenda.
          %p
            The elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D X
            are called
            %strong finite distributions
            or
            %strong
              finitely-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} supported
              probability measures
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#pushforward Pushforward
          %p
            Given a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            %strong pushforward
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f:D X\to D Y
            as follows. Given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in D X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D f)(p)\in D Y
            is the function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y \;\mapsto\; \sum_{x\in f^{-1}(y)} p(x) .
          %p (Note that, up to zero addenda, the sum above is again finite.)
          %p
            Compare with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushforward+of+measures"} pushforward of measures
          %p
            This makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#monad_structure Monad structure
          %p
            The unit map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta:X\to D X
            maps the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            to the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_x:X\to[0,1]
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo =
                            %mi x
                            %mo ;
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mo ≠
                            %mi x
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta_x(y) \;=\; \begin{cases}
                  1 &amp; y=x ;\\
                  0 &amp; y\ne x .
                  \\end{cases}
          %p
            Compare with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measures"} Dirac measures
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+valuation#dirac_valuation"} valuations
          %p
            The multiplication map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E:D D X\to D X
            maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi\in D D X
            to the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\xi\in D X
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                      %mi X
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E\xi(x) \;=\; \sum_{p\in D X} p(x) \, \xi(p).
          %p (Note that, up to zero addenda, the sum above is once again finite.)
          %p
            The maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            satisfy the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            laws. The resulting monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D,E,\delta)
            is known as
            = succeed "," do
              %strong distribution monad
            %strong finitary Giry monad
            (in analogy with the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            = succeed "," do
              %strong convex combination monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D X
            can be interpreted as formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex combinations
            of elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This can be seen as a discrete, finitary analogue of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monad"} probability monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrals"} integrals
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sums"} sums
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+spaces"} convex spaces
            %li
              %p
                The monad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+monad"} finitary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monad"} commutative
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+morphisms"} Kleisli morphisms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                are (finitary)
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    stochastic maps
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/stochastic+maps"} ?
          %p (…)
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"}> convex space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+space"} conical space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+of+probability%2C+measures%2C+and+valuations"} monads of probability, measures, and valuations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"}> Giry monad
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    probabilistic powerdomain
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/probabilistic+powerdomain"} ?
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+probabilistic+powerdomain"} extended probabilistic powerdomain
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"}> monad
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+%28in+computer+science%29"} monad (in computer science)
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Fritz"} Tobias Fritz
                and
